#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-AD0210 expect=skipped domain=ADSL
#note "THE SHAPE THIS PLAN GATES. ADSL carries NO ARM while DM does. Until 2026-09-21 the unqualified ARM resolved OUT OF THE JOIN, so the check read DM.ARM != DM.ARM -- always false, the rule structurally unable to fire. PLAN-unqualified-name-primary-only made an unqualified name mean the PRIMARY always, which turned the same shape into an OVER-FIRE: the absent ADSL column folds to a broadcast constant (the empty string) and differs from DM.ARM on every candidate row. => The rule now DECLARES the bare ARM in Requirements.Variables.All, so an ADSL without it SKIPS -- 0 findings by an auditable route. Verdict 2-1' per CORE-RULES-AUTHORING-GUIDELINES 4.4: the absence is itself a finding and is reported by CDISC-AD0071 (co-present in every adamig package this rule ships into). Do NOT 'fix' this by giving ADSL the column: -valid-ADSL.cdt already covers present-and-agreeing and -invalid-ADSL.cdt present-and-disagreeing. This file is the third shape, and the only one the engine change moved."
dataset ADSL
col STUDYID type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col SAFFL   type=Char
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | Y
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1023 | Y
---

dataset DM label=Demographics
col STUDYID type=Char
col DOMAIN  type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col ARM     type=Char
---
CDISCPILOT01 | DM | 01-701-1015 | Placebo
CDISCPILOT01 | DM | 01-701-1023 | Placebo
---
